<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for the oam macOS binaries. Signed in by
  scripts/lib/mac-signing.sh (mac_sign_binary) on every mac release leg, and
  checked back out of the signature by mac_verify_binary, which requires
  EXACTLY these three keys, each true.

  - allow-jit, allow-unsigned-executable-memory: V8 compiles JavaScript and
    WebAssembly to executable memory at runtime. Without them the hardened
    runtime kills the process at the first JIT, not at startup, which is why
    scripts/fixtures/jit-smoke.js runs against the signed binary.
  - disable-library-validation: OAM_ENABLE_NATIVE_ADDONS=1 loads third-party
    .node addons, which never carry our signature.

  Do not add get-task-allow (notarization rejects it) or copy Node's or Bun's
  supersets. This set must stay a subset of Yaw Terminal's, which re-signs the
  oam it bundles.

  Editing this comment: no double hyphen, no angle brackets, no ampersand.
  codesign reads this file with a stricter parser than plutil, and
  scripts/test-scripts.sh fails on any of them.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
